a{color:#d5bbff}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}li{margin:.45rem 0}
</style>
<main>
<h1>Dreamcore Dungeons privacy notice</h1>
<p>Notice version: <strong>2026-11-09.3</strong></p>
<h2>Who is responsible?</h2>
<address>Fabian Ceolotto<br>Fröhlichgasse 83/16<br>8010 Graz, Austria<br>Privacy requests: <a href="mailto:fabeceo@gmail.com">fabeceo@gmail.com</a></address>
<h2>Optional playtest sharing</h2>
<p>Participation in playtest data sharing is for adults aged 18 or older. We ask for a self-confirmation, not your date of birth or an identity document. You can play without sharing. If you opt in, I use your playtest data to investigate bugs, improve the game and compare builds. The legal basis for optional sharing is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR). This includes storing the optional upload queue and diagnostic history in your browser. Your choice, notice version and decision time are remembered. Ordinary game saves and settings serve a separate purpose.</p>
<ul>
<li>Runs: game build and rules version, progress and outcomes, timestamps, choices, character builds, skills, items, and snapshots of game state.</li>
<li>Technical reports: error text and recent technical events, browser/device details such as user agent and window size, and game/loading context. Reports can include information you write yourself. Leave out personal information and secrets.</li>
<li>A random installation ID and session/run IDs connect records; no player account is required. These records are treated as pseudonymous. The browser keeps a private credential used to authenticate uploads and deletion requests.</li>
</ul>
<p>With automatic sharing off, you can explicitly send a one-time problem report. That action authorizes sending the description and accompanying technical context, and storing it locally until delivery can be retried. It does not enable automatic sharing. You can review or export local diagnostic information separately; manually sharing an exported file sends it to the recipient you choose.</p>
<h2>Hosting and recipients</h2>
<p>GitHub Pages hosts the game and logs visitor IP addresses for security, independently of your sharing choice. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages">GitHub’s hosting information</a> and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>.</p>
<p>Cloudflare Workers receives reports and uses request information, including IP addresses to limit abuse during registration. I rely on my legitimate interest in securing this service for that rate limiting (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare D1 stores the reports on my behalf. I am the only operator with access to the private Observatory.</p>
<p>D1 currently runs in Western Europe. Cloudflare may process data outside the European Economic Area; I do not guarantee EU-only processing. Cloudflare’s <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/terms/#6-data-processing-and-security">Self-Serve terms</a> incorporate its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/">Data Processing Addendum</a>, which describes applicable safeguards for restricted transfers, including <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-scc/">EU Standard Contractual Clauses</a>. Contact me to request information or a copy of the safeguards that apply to your data.</p>
<p>If you email me about your data, I use your email address and the information needed to handle the request and document my response, as required by Article 6(1)(c) GDPR. The contact mailbox is hosted by Gmail. Please leave out passwords and private upload credentials.</p>
<h2>How long data is kept</h2>
<p>Ordinary uploaded records and unfinished upload parts are eligible for daily cleanup after 90 days. I review whether each reference run and its supporting records are still needed within 12 months of the run’s first recording, and at least annually thereafter while kept as a reference. If there is no continuing need, I remove the reference designation so the ordinary cleanup applies, or delete the data sooner. The review is a check, not a guaranteed deletion date.</p>
<p>The daily cleanup also deletes installation records older than 90 days once there are no reports, runs or upload parts left for that installation. I review separate issue notes and exports for deletion when they are no longer needed or when handling a deletion request. Cloudflare D1 Free can restore earlier database states for up to seven days using <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/reference/time-travel/">Time Travel</a>. A deletion from active storage does not immediately remove earlier restore points.</p>
<p>The browser upload/history store has a 20 MiB cap. You can clear its data from the game or browser; clearing browser storage can remove the credential needed to delete online records yourself.</p>
<h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
<p>Go to Settings → Playtest &amp; feedback to turn sharing off. Withdrawal stops automatic sharing, clears local playtest history and queued reports, and requests deletion of active server records linked to this browser installation. It does not change the lawfulness of earlier processing. “Delete my collected data” also works for reports sent while automatic sharing was off. If offline, the browser keeps the deletion request and the credential needed to carry it out; it retries when the game page is open and connected. New sharing is blocked until the server confirms deletion. Keep this browser’s data until deletion is confirmed. If deletion cannot be verified or you no longer have the original browser, contact me at the address above. The local download includes retained local records only.</p>
<p>You may request access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability where applicable. You may also object where processing is based on legitimate interests, and lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://dsb.gv.at/">Austrian Data Protection Authority</a> or another competent supervisory authority.</p>
<p><a href="./">Back to the game</a></p>
<h2>Optional profile name and public Nightmare highscores</h2>
<p>Public-score consent version: <strong>2026-11-12.1</strong>. Reading the list does not enable playtest sharing. You may choose a nickname; otherwise your assigned Player number is displayed. Names need not be unique. Your chosen name is stored on this device and, while playtest sharing is enabled, with your browser installation on the server.</p>
<p>The separate, initially unchecked “Share my future Nightmare highscores” choice allows future completed Nightmare scores to appear publicly with your profile name or Player number, heroine, tier and active clear time. Old private scores remain private. This additional publication is based on your optional consent. Internal installation and run identifiers, equipment, seeds and diagnostic reports are not included.</p>
<p>Turning this choice off stops future publication and requests removal of previous public scores, even while private playtest sharing stays on. A new opt-in never republishes old scores. Your name or assigned Player number can link your public scores together. Turning playtest sharing off or deleting collected data also requests deletion of uploaded scores. Offline deletion waits for a connection. Cached public lists may show deleted scores for at most 60 seconds after successful online deletion. Normal retention still applies.</p>
</main>
</html>
